class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: net.parse_ip and net.parse_address read IPv4's dotted decimal without leading zeros and IPv6's groups, compressed, in either case and with an IPv4 tail, and read a zone after an IPv6 address as written, and refuse an empty or overlong zone, one holding a NUL, a zone after an IPv4 address, a stray colon, a second ::, an overlong group and a port past 65535 as invalid_address; net.append_ip and net.append_address write them back as RFC 5952 does, lower case with the longest zero run shortened, an IPv4-mapped address in dotted decimal and the zone after a %, an IPv6 address and its zone bracketed before its port, each read back as the same address; net.with_zone gives and takes away a zone, refusing one for IPv4, and net.same_address tells two zones apart; the constructors compare as they should, text.format writes an address, and an address that does not fit a builder writes nothing
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
status: 42
constructs: 0520, 0570, 0640, 0790, 0900, 1030, 1210
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, linux-rv64, darwin-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64
